BT /F2 9.7 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 745.0 Tm (9. What produces the 'a' wave in a normal jugular venous pulse tracing?) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.3 Tf 0.1 0.33 0.58 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 728.3 Tm (Answer: A. Right atrial contraction.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 712.0 Tm (Explanation: The a wave reflects the rise in right atrial pressure during atrial systole. It occurs immediately) Tj ET
