BT /F1 7.2 Tf 0.43 0.45 0.49 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 642.6 Tm (Source: circulation-1:Q67 | 24-25) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.7 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 619.4 Tm (10. Why is perfusion of the left ventricular myocardium predominantly diastolic?) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.3 Tf 0.1 0.33 0.58 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 602.7 Tm (Answer: A. Ventricular contraction compresses intramural vessels.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 586.4 Tm (Explanation: High left ventricular wall tension during systole squeezes intramyocardial coronary vessels;) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 573.3 Tm (relaxation permits better flow.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.4 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 557.2 Tm (Not B: Coronary ostia remain open through the cardiac cycle.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.4 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 543.8 Tm (Not C: Aortic pressure persists during diastole and drives coronary flow.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.4 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 530.4 Tm (Not D: Coronary flow increases during relaxation rather than disappearing.) Tj ET
BT /F1 7.2 Tf 0.43 0.45 0.49 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 517.0 Tm (Source: lecture-6:Q22 | 27; Chapter 23 ?3) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.7 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 493.8 Tm (11. Beta-1 adrenergic stimulation generally increases ventricular contractility through which sequence?) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.3 Tf 0.1 0.33 0.58 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 477.1 Tm (Answer: B. Increased cAMP/PKA signalling -> greater calcium availability.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 460.8 Tm (Explanation: Beta-1 signalling raises cAMP and PKA activity, enhancing calcium entry and cycling for stronger) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 447.7 Tm (contraction.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.4 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 431.6 Tm (Not A: Blocking release channels would reduce systolic calcium release.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.4 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 418.2 Tm (Not C: Vagal slowing is not the main ventricular inotropic pathway.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.4 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 404.8 Tm (Not D: Beta-1 stimulation raises, not lowers, cAMP.) Tj ET
BT /F1 7.2 Tf 0.43 0.45 0.49 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 391.4 Tm (Source: circulation-1:Q10 | 46-47; Chapter 2 ?7) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.7 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 368.2 Tm (12. What principle allows an electromagnetic flowmeter to determine vascular flow?) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.3 Tf 0.1 0.33 0.58 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 351.5 Tm (Answer: A. Moving conductive blood induces voltage in a magnetic field.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 335.2 Tm (Explanation: Conducting blood moving through a magnetic field induces a voltage that can be used to estimate its) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 322.1 Tm (velocity and flow.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.4 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 306.0 Tm (Not B: That describes neither the electromagnetic principle nor Fick correctly.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.4 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 292.6 Tm (Not C: Korotkoff sounds estimate arterial blood pressure, not direct flow.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.4 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 279.2 Tm (Not D: Tracer approaches are distinct from electromagnetic flow measurement.) Tj ET
BT /F1 7.2 Tf 0.43 0.45 0.49 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 265.8 Tm (Source: circulation-1:Q57 | 62) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.7 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 242.6 Tm (13. A person lying still stands up, then begins walking. What feature makes the calf-muscle pump effective?) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.3 Tf 0.1 0.33 0.58 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 225.9 Tm (Answer: C. Deep vein compression with one-way valves.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 209.6 Tm (Explanation: Calf contractions compress deep veins, while competent venous valves favour upward flow toward the) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 196.5 Tm (heart instead of backflow.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.4 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 180.4 Tm (Not A: Venous return requires directed pressure gradients, not dilation alone.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.4 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 167.0 Tm (Not B: Capillaries do not function as contractile muscle pumps.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.4 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 153.6 Tm (Not D: Arteries do not rely on venous-style one-way valves.) Tj ET
