BT /F2 12.0 Tf 1 1 1 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 815.0 Tm (DOMiNANCE / CVS PHYSIOLOGY) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 1 1 1 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 798.0 Tm (MOCK 03 | 60Q | EXPLANATION GUIDE | 90 MIN) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.7 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 745.0 Tm (24. What effect does activating alpha-adrenoceptors have on vessels supplying the myocardium?) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.3 Tf 0.1 0.33 0.58 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 728.3 Tm (Answer: A. Coronary vasoconstriction.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 712.0 Tm (Explanation: The lecture identifies coronary alpha-receptor stimulation as directly vasoconstricting, distinct) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 698.9 Tm (from metabolic vasodilation. Local metabolic signals can still override this direct constrictor tendency during) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 685.8 Tm (increased myocardial work.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.4 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 669.7 Tm (Not B: Metabolic dilation is driven largely by myocardial activity and metabolites.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.4 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 656.3 Tm (Not C: Oxygen extraction is a tissue process, not a direct receptor effect.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.4 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 642.9 Tm (Not D: Increased contractility is associated with cardiac beta-adrenergic stimulation.) Tj ET
BT /F1 7.2 Tf 0.43 0.45 0.49 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 629.5 Tm (Source: lecture-6:Q24 | 28) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.7 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 606.3 Tm (25. Redness spreads beyond a stroked patch of skin as the flare develops. What generates this spread?) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.3 Tf 0.1 0.33 0.58 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 589.6 Tm (Answer: D. Antidromic impulses in branches of a sensory axon.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 573.3 Tm (Explanation: The flare is an axon reflex: sensory-nerve branches release vasodilator neuropeptides in surrounding) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 560.2 Tm (skin without a spinal reflex.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.4 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 544.1 Tm (Not A: Lymphatic filtration does not produce this arteriolar flare.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.4 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 530.7 Tm (Not B: The surrounding redness is functional vasodilation, not thrombosis.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.4 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 517.3 Tm (Not C: A central synaptic reflex is not needed for the axon reflex.) Tj ET
BT /F1 7.2 Tf 0.43 0.45 0.49 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 503.9 Tm (Source: lecture-6:Q51 | 40) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.7 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 480.7 Tm (26. A nurse notices ankle swelling after a long standing shift. Which immediate local change promotes this) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.7 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 467.0 Tm (swelling?) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.3 Tf 0.1 0.33 0.58 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 450.3 Tm (Answer: D. Raised capillary pressure increases outward filtration.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 434.0 Tm (Explanation: The increased hydrostatic pressure in dependent leg capillaries pushes more fluid into the) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 420.9 Tm (interstitium and promotes oedema.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.4 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 404.8 Tm (Not A: A lower capillary pressure would oppose outward filtration.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.4 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 391.4 Tm (Not B: Standing promotes dependent filtration; it does not stop capillary exchange.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.4 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 378.0 Tm (Not C: Plasma oncotic pressure ordinarily favours fluid retention within blood.) Tj ET
BT /F1 7.2 Tf 0.43 0.45 0.49 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 364.6 Tm (Source: circulation-3:Q4 | Circulation 3, slide 3; Chapter 19 ?2) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.7 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 341.4 Tm (27. During exercise, sympathetic activity increases throughout the body, yet working muscle receives much) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.7 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 327.7 Tm (more blood. Which explanation is best?) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.3 Tf 0.1 0.33 0.58 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 311.0 Tm (Answer: C. Local metabolic dilation outweighs constriction in active muscle.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 294.7 Tm (Explanation: Active muscle generates enough vasodilator metabolites to oppose sympathetic constriction,) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 281.6 Tm (redirecting blood to the tissue that needs it.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.4 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 265.5 Tm (Not A: Sympathetic activity often remains elevated; metabolites oppose its constrictor effect locally.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.4 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 252.1 Tm (Not B: Constriction does not raise flow equally across every organ.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.4 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 238.7 Tm (Not D: Metabolites in working muscle predominantly dilate its arterioles.) Tj ET
BT /F1 7.2 Tf 0.43 0.45 0.49 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 225.3 Tm (Source: circulation-2:Q18 | 2-3, 5-6, 11) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.7 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 202.1 Tm (28. A low-frequency third heart sound occurs in early diastole. What ventricular event coincides with it?) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.3 Tf 0.1 0.33 0.58 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 185.4 Tm (Answer: C. Rapid passive ventricular filling.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 169.1 Tm (Explanation: S3 occurs during rapid early-diastolic ventricular filling, as blood entering the chamber causes) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 156.0 Tm (vibrations.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.4 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 139.9 Tm (Not A: Atrial depolarisation precedes the atrial contribution later in diastole.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.4 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 126.5 Tm (Not B: Isovolumetric contraction occurs near S1.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.4 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 113.1 Tm (Not D: Aortic valve opening occurs during ventricular systole.) Tj ET
BT /F1 7.2 Tf 0.43 0.45 0.49 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 99.7 Tm (Source: circulation-1:Q29 | 28) Tj ET
