BT /F2 9.7 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 745.0 Tm (59. A patient with coronary atheroma is comfortable at rest but develops exertional chest pain. Which) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.7 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 731.3 Tm (explanation fits best?) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.3 Tf 0.1 0.33 0.58 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 714.6 Tm (Answer: B. Restricted coronary flow reserve cannot meet increased demand.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 698.3 Tm (Explanation: A narrowed vessel may deliver adequate resting flow but cannot dilate enough to meet exercise demand,) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 685.2 Tm (causing reversible ischaemia.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.4 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 669.1 Tm (Not A: Plaque does not disappear with exertion.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.4 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 655.7 Tm (Not C: Exercise raises myocardial work and oxygen requirements.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.4 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 642.3 Tm (Not D: Resting coronary flow may be sufficient despite reduced reserve.) Tj ET
BT /F1 7.2 Tf 0.43 0.45 0.49 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 628.9 Tm (Source: lecture-6:Q27 | 29; Chapter 23 ?6) Tj ET
