BT /F2 9.3 Tf 0.1 0.33 0.58 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 575.3 Tm (Answer: B. 0.10 s, within the expected P-wave duration.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 559.0 Tm (Explanation: At 25 mm/s a small square equals 0.04 s. Thus 2.5 x 0.04 = 0.10 s, at the upper end of the stated) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 545.9 Tm (0.08-0.10 s range.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.4 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 529.8 Tm (Not A: The calculation uses only one small square rather than 2.5 squares.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.4 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 516.4 Tm (Not C: This assigns 0.08 s to each small square, twice its actual time.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.4 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 503.0 Tm (Not D: This incorrectly assigns 0.10 s to each small square.) Tj ET
